{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoding","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPTransport","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13HTTPTransportP"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The wire shape, for a server that ingests these batches:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One request per batch, in the order the delivery hands them over, the next batch sent only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once the previous one is delivered or dropped."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The method is ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the URL is the configured endpoint.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The header fields are the configured ones, then the trace context of the batch’s first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record, then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":", each replacing fields of the same name before it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The instrument injects the first (oldest) record’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/context"},{"text":", so a server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extracting it joins the request, and the events, to the trace the app was in. Its field","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names are the instrument’s: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traceparent"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracestate"},{"text":" for a W3C Trace Context tracer.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record tracked outside any span, or an instrument that injects nothing (the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoOpInstrument"},{"text":" when none is bootstrapped), adds no fields.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only the first record’s context travels in the header fields, though a batch may hold","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records tracked in other traces. A server that needs each record’s context reads it from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the body, where a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" writes it.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType"},{"type":"text","text":", whatever a configured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field or the instrument wrote."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is exactly the encoder’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/body"},{"type":"text","text":" for the batch’s records, oldest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first. The format is the encoder’s; events need no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A response with a 2xx status means the batch arrived."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A request the transport can never send ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError\/invalidRequest(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":": a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"malformed or unsupported URL, or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http"},{"type":"text","text":" URL App Transport Security refuses) isn’t sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No response, a 5xx status, 408 Request Timeout or 429 Too Many Requests means it didn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrive yet: the same request is sent again after the backoff’s next wait, for as long as it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes. A "},{"code":"Retry-After","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" field is not read; the backoff alone sets the wait."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any other status means the endpoint won’t take the batch, and it isn’t sent again.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record can arrive twice: a request the server took whose response was lost is sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again, and a record a store redelivers after the app was stopped mid-send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":") may have arrived before. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the one it was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first sent with, so an encoder that writes each record’s identifier lets the server keep one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns once the batch is delivered, dropped, or the delivery is cancelled, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a tracker’s store keeps the records of a batch until it arrives, and a batch still being"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retried when the app ends is delivered again on the next launch. A batch the endpoint rejects,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose request can’t be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped: logged at error"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level and reported on "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":". Each failed attempt that will be retried is logged at notice level."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Cancelling the delivery cancels the send in flight or the wait before the next one, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns without logging or reporting it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While a batch is retried, the delivery’s later batches wait in this destination’s buffer,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which drops its oldest batch when full ("},{"code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): offline for long"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enough, the batches dropped there are lost to this run. A store never had them acknowledged,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so it delivers them on the next launch; without a store they are gone."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder())","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as one request, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sends it again until it arrives."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:encoder:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:transport:encoder:backoff:clock:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinati